{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"primordial-nosophobic-aruanas","creation_channel":"cli","description":"`scripts/` (41 files) is excluded from every static gate: `Makefile:11` sets `sources = src tests`,\nso `make lint` never sees it, and `Makefile:205` runs `mypy src/rebar`, so `make typecheck` never\nsees it either. `ruff check scripts/` today reports **78 violations**.\n\nBlast radius is low — this workflow tooling is not shipped to clients — but seven of these files are\ninvoked directly by `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, the blocking workflow behind the\n`Verified` vote: `check_verify_gate_parity.py` (:130), `check_comment_hygiene.py` (:144),\n`check_raw_git_writes.py` (:162), `check_wall_clock_asserts.py` (:176), `gen_env_registry.py` (:419),\n`check_docs_index.py` (:441), `check_readme_quickstart.py` (:452). The gate implementations are\nthemselves ungated.\n\n## The 28 substantive violations\n\n| Rule | n | Nature |\n|---|---|---|\n| `RUF100` unused-noqa | 12 | Dead directives; `ruff --fix` removes them |\n| `E501` line-too-long | 11 | Rewrap; no behavior |\n| `RUF005` collection-concat | 2 | `prefix + [x]` -> `[*prefix, x]`; both in `check_complexity_baseline.py:181,187` |\n| `RUF059` unused unpack | 2 | `jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py:212,222` — `b1`/`b2` captured, never read |\n| `B905` zip without `strict=` | 1 | `check_wall_clock_asserts.py:101` |\n\n**No live defect is present in this set.** Two candidates were checked and cleared:\n\n- `B905` at `check_wall_clock_asserts.py:101` is `zip(sub.ops, sub.comparators)` over an\n  `ast.Compare`. Those lists are equal-length by construction (`a < b < c` yields `ops=[Lt,Lt]`,\n  `comparators=[b,c]`), so the silent-truncation failure mode cannot occur. `strict=True` is correct\n  as hardening, not a fix.\n- The two `RUF059` sites capture an HTTP response body the probe deliberately does not inspect\n  (read-back is a separate `_req` call). `_`-prefix them.\n\nThe `RUF100` count is itself the argument for the gate: 12 `noqa` directives are dead *because*\nnothing lints the directory. Five reference rules not in `select` (`PLC0415`, `S603`, `S310`,\n`PLR0915`) — confirm none documents a live intent before deleting.\n\n## The 50 T201 (print) violations — exempt, do not fix\n\nPrint discipline in local workflow tooling is low value, and these scripts' prints are their output.\nThey sit in 10 files with no `per-file-ignores` entry: `calibrate_completion_floor.py` (11),\n`check_verify_gate_parity.py` (7), `verify_mcp_publisher_pin.py` (6), `check_raw_git_writes.py` (6),\n`t5c_calibrate.py` (5), `check_wall_clock_asserts.py` (5), `check_commit_message_wrap.py` (4),\n`check_build_env_locked.py` (3), `check_dco_identity.py` (2), `normalize_ci_conclusion.py` (1).\n\n**Resolve with ONE whole-directory entry `\"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\"]`, replacing the nine existing\nsingle-file `scripts/*.py` entries** (`pyproject.toml:461,465,468,471,475,479,483,487,491`). This\ntakes `per-file-ignores` from 17 entries to 9 and converts the scripts exemption from nine\ndiscretionary per-file entries into a single INVARIANT whole-directory one — the same shape as\n`\"tests/**\"`, which the config already marks PERMANENT. It shrinks and hardens the allowlist rather\nthan growing it. Adding ten NEW single-file entries instead is explicitly rejected.\n\n## Risk\n\nLow. 25 of the 28 are provably zero-behavior. The remaining 3 need a reviewer who reads the\nsurrounding logic rather than the diff, and `check_complexity_baseline.py` is a gate whose own\ncorrectness is being edited.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All 12 `RUF100`, 11 `E501`, 2 `RUF005`, 2 `RUF059` and 1 `B905` violations in `scripts/` are\n      resolved\n- [ ] Any deleted `noqa` referencing a non-enabled rule is confirmed to document no live intent\n- [ ] The nine single-file `scripts/*.py` T201 entries are replaced by one `\"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\"]`;\n      `per-file-ignores` has FEWER entries after this change than before\n- [ ] `scripts/` is added to the lint scope (`Makefile` `sources`) so `make lint` covers it, and CI\n      is green on the result\n- [ ] The seven CI-invoked gate scripts behave identically: verified by a CI run, not inspection\n- [ ] A follow-up ticket records the remaining `mypy` gap (`make typecheck` is `mypy src/rebar`;\n      `scripts/` and `tests/` are untyped)","id":"ae96-f114-5363-4d57","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","priority":2,"tags":["janitor"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Lint scripts/ in CI: clear the 28 substantive violations, consolidate the T201 exemption"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786054534043576001,"uuid":"0efa87b0-c210-4de2-9423-0535668712f1"}